## Summary
Functionally correct but will not scale. Performance issues with large datasets.

## Critical Issues (must fix before merge)

### 1. Loading All Products Into Memory — PERFORMANCE
`Product.findAll()` loads every product into memory before filtering.
With 100K+ products, this will:
- Cause memory spikes
- Timeout on large datasets
- Block the event loop during filtering

Fix: Push filtering to the database:
```typescript
router.get('/search', async (req, res) => {
  const { q, category, minPrice, maxPrice } = req.query;

  const where: any = {};

  if (q) {
    where.OR = [
      { name: { contains: q, mode: 'insensitive' } },
      { description: { contains: q, mode: 'insensitive' } }
    ];
  }

  if (category) where.category = category;
  if (minPrice) where.price = { ...where.price, gte: Number(minPrice) };
  if (maxPrice) where.price = { ...where.price, lte: Number(maxPrice) };

  const products = await Product.findMany({ where, take: 50 });
  res.json({ data: products });
});
```

### 2. No Pagination — PERFORMANCE
Returns all matching products without limit.
A search matching 10K products will return 10K objects.

Fix: Add pagination:
```typescript
const page = Number(req.query.page) || 1;
const limit = Math.min(Number(req.query.limit) || 20, 100);
const offset = (page - 1) * limit;

const [products, total] = await Promise.all([
  Product.findMany({ where, skip: offset, take: limit }),
  Product.count({ where })
]);

res.json({ 
  data: products, 
  pagination: { page, limit, total, pages: Math.ceil(total / limit) }
});
```

